{
  "_doc": "The reflect contract, captured from the PYTHON kernel's own replies (src/lib/python, `kernel/_agent.py` `_apply_reflect_flags` / `_roster`) and reproduced by the ts kernel (tests/reflect.test.ts replays every case from `tree` + `bundles`). DISTILLED by default: `tree` is the roster {id, sentence, description?, mode?, children} (whole: a reflect that passes the gate returns the tree whole), no verb docs (they are the `docs` kernel verb); `detail:\"full\"` gives the wiring tree. `tree` is decided by key presence (absent = all, null/none = omitted), `tree:\"ids\"` and `bundles` page with `limit`/`after` (`next` / `bundles_next`), `readme` is true | \"index\" | \"<key>\" (this kernel's doc tree is empty). Differences BY DESIGN, per runtime: the root's `runtime` (\"ts\") and handler_module; the kernel verbs this kernel answers (no tree CRUD — the `_` line says so); the bundle catalog; python's root also carries its loader's doc frame (`self_extension`, and `readmes`/`docs` under full), which this kernel has no loader to contribute. The browser kernel has no OS env, so env is always \"host\" and version null.",
  "bundles": [
    "terminal_view.js",
    "canvas.js"
  ],
